    "final_text": "I've built the todo CLI with all four commands working. The full suite (201 tests) passes on three consecutive runs and ESLint is clean. The work is on branch `feat/cli-todo-app` in 6 commits.\n\n**Try it:**\n```\nnode index.js add \"Buy groceries\"   \u2192 Added todo 1: Buy groceries\nnode index.js list                  \u2192 1. [ ] Buy groceries\n                                      1 todo: 0 done, 1 pending\nnode index.js complete 1            \u2192 Completed todo 1: Buy groceries\nnode index.js delete 1              \u2192 Deleted todo 1: Buy groceries\n```\n\n**How it's organized:** `index.js` is just the entry point. The logic is split across `src/`: command handling (`cli.js`), the todo operations (`todos.js`, which never touches the disk), reading and writing the file (`storage.js`), and list output (`format.js`). There are no runtime dependencies. The README explains the design decisions.\n\n**Choices I made where the spec was silent:**\n- **File format:** `todos.json` holds `{ \"nextId\": N, \"todos\": [...] }` rather than a bare array, so a deleted id is never handed out again. Otherwise, deleting todo 3 and adding a new one would reuse 3. A file containing a bare array still loads. The catch is that anything reading `todos.json` directly and expecting a plain array won't work.\n- **Exit codes:** 0 for success, 1 when the command can't be carried out (id not found, corrupt file), 2 for incorrect usage (missing argument, unknown command, an id like `abc`).\n- **Completing a todo twice** prints a note and exits 0.\n- **Text** is trimmed, capped at 500 characters, and can't contain newlines or other control characters, which also blocks terminal escape codes. Unquoted words are joined: `add Buy milk` works.\n- **Safety:** each write goes to a temporary file that then replaces `todos.json`, so a crash can't leave a half-written file. A lock file stops two commands running at once from losing each other's changes. A corrupt `todos.json` is reported and left untouched.\n- **Limits:** the text limit and the lock timeouts can be changed with the `TODO_*` environment variables listed in the README.\n\n**Testing:** the tests are split into seven files, from unit tests up to end-to-end runs of `node index.js`. They cover missing arguments, invalid and unknown ids, the empty list, corrupt files, unicode text, length limits and parallel processes. To check the tests actually catch bugs, I planted 12 deliberate bugs in the code (removing the lock, reusing ids, swapping `[x]` and `[ ]`, and so on). Each one made at least one test fail.\n\n**Bugs I found and fixed while reviewing my own code:**\n- `node index.js list | head -1` on a long list crashed with an error dump when `head` stopped reading. It now exits quietly with code 0, and a test covers it.\n- The lock retry loop could keep waiting past its timeout if other commands kept taking and releasing the lock.\n- Lock creation could leave a lock file behind and report the wrong error if writing it failed partway.\n\n**Not done:**\n- Nothing was pushed because the repo has no git remote.\n- The `humanizer` skill and `dx run-gate` that CLAUDE.md mentions aren't available here. I followed the humanizer's writing guidelines by hand and ran the tests directly.\n- Commits use the `Co-Authored-By: Dex` line because a project hook asked for it.\n- I left `CLAUDE.md` uncommitted since it's your file.",
